120:Echo Operator registers a validating webhook, a mutating webhook, and a conversion webhook on a shared TLS server. The webhook server listens on port 8443 by default and is exposed through the Helm Service on port 443.
122:### Validating webhook
131:### Mutating webhook
138:### Conversion webhook
163:- `WEBHOOK_PORT` - port for the TLS webhook server, default `8443`
173:## Helm webhook values
175:The chart supports these webhook-related values in `values.yaml`:
178:webhook:
182:  createWebhookConfigurations: false   # set true to pre-create webhook configs via Helm
187:    secretName: echo-operator-webhook-tls
194:The TLS Secret must be created outside the chart by a cluster admin or external tooling. When `createWebhookConfigurations` is `false` (the default), the operator self-registers its admission webhook configurations on startup.
143:- `example.com/v1alpha2` is the storage version and adds `spec.logLevel`.
145:`EchoConverter` converts between versions. When converting from `v1alpha1` to `v1alpha2`, `logLevel` defaults to `INFO`. When converting from `v1alpha2` to `v1alpha1`, `logLevel` is dropped.
154:@Version(value = "v1alpha2", storage = true, served = true)
196:## Example CR for v1alpha2
198:You can also create a `v1alpha2` CR:
201:apiVersion: example.com/v1alpha2
206:  message: "Hello from v1alpha2"
217:Because `v1alpha2` is the storage version, reading the resource back will show `apiVersion: example.com/v1alpha2` and `spec.logLevel`.
